From 586288c0571f58942acc18b4a9084b950062ad02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juanan <juanan@test.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:03:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] T9: validator corrections until publication and
 publication guard

Client change request after v1.0.0 (v1.1.0):
- Publication uses the marking workflow of mod_assign: until the grade is
  released the student sees nothing and the gradebook is empty.
- New state "validated, pending publication": the validator can correct
  the validated grade as many times as needed until it is released; once
  released nobody can change it. Each correction keeps the original
  teacher grade, stores the latest validator grade (validated values,
  validator and time only move when a criterion changes) and triggers
  grade_validation_updated with the previous and new values.
- Publication guard (observer of workflow_state_updated): a grade cannot
  be released before it is validated, from the grading form, quick
  grading or the bulk action; it is set back to "Ready for release",
  removed from the gradebook, and grade_publication_blocked is triggered.
- Without the marking workflow the v1.0.0 rules apply and the grading
  form warns that grades reach the students as soon as they are saved.
- Version 2024112202 (2024112200-ied2); PATCHES.md: roles, workflow
  setup and new limitations.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
